olor.\n    rs = list(range(1, h - 1, 4))\n    cs = list(range(0, w - 1, 5))\n    return [[3 if grid[r][c] == 7 else grid[r][c] for c in cs] for r in rs]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":78,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793545538.507,"t1":1793545551.737,"alias":"task-4bcb43b3","message":"Your program was checked on earlier pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n4 8 8 8 4 8\n5 4 4 4 1 4\n4 8 8 8 4 8\n4 8 8 8 4 8\n4 8 8 8 4 8\nwhere the pair's output is\n5 8 8 8 8 1\n8 8 8 8 8 8\n1 8 0 8 8 8\n8 8 8 0 8 9\nFailed checks in this instance: 3 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find the repeating horizontal and vertical grid-line spacing from\n    # the most frequent non-background color runs.\n    # The cells are 5 rows by 4 columns in the first demo, and 4 by 5\n    # in the current input; infer the lattice from repeated line patterns.\n    row_lines = [r for r in range(h) if len(set(grid[r])) > 1]\n    col_lines = [c for c in range(w) if len({grid[r][c] for r in range(h)}) > 1]\n\n    def spacing(indices):\n        diffs = [b - a for a, b in zip(indices, indices[1:])]\n        return max(set(diffs), key=diffs.count) if diffs else 1\n\n    # Use rows/columns whose patterns identify the colored intersection lines.\n    # For these patterned grids, the lines repeat at a regular period.\n    dr = spacing(row_lines)\n    dc = spacing(col_lines)\n    r0 = row_lines[0] if row_lines else 0\n    c0 = col_lines[0] if col_lines else 0\n\n    # The output records the lattice intersections, replacing unmarked\n    # intersections with the dominant interior fill color.\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    background = max(counts, key=counts.get)\n    fill_counts = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row if v != background)\n    fill = max(fill_counts, key=fill_counts.get) if fill_counts else background\n\n    rows = list(range(r0, h, dr))\n    cols = list(range(c0, w, dc))\n    return [[grid[r][c] if grid[r][c] != background else fill for c in cols] for r in rows]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"valid":true}},{"step":78,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1793545551.862,"t1":1793545564.392,"alias":"task-4bcb43b3","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT. Wrong attempts so far: 1.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-4bcb43b3\nTest input (27x22):\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\nWrong attempts used: 1/8. Demo requests used: 1/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find the repeating separator rows/columns: they are predominantly\n    # the separator color, with occasional colored marks at intersections.\n    def line_score_row(r):\n        return sum(v in (4, 5, 6, 9, 0, 1, 3, 7) for v in grid[r])\n\n    # These grids use regular periods; infer the row/column line phases\n    # by looking for rows and columns with a color different from the fill.\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    fill = counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n    row_candidates = [r for r, row in enumerate(grid) if sum(v != fill for v in row) > w // 2]\n    col_candidates = [c for c in range(w) if sum(grid[r][c] != fill for r in range(h)) > h // 2]\n\n    def period(vals):\n        ds = [b-a for a, b in zip(vals, vals[1:])]\n        return Counter(ds).most_common(1)[0][0] if ds else 1\n\n    rp = period(row_candidates)\n    cp = period(col_candidates)\n    r0 = row_candidates[0] if row_candidates else 0\n    c0 = col_candidates[0] if col_candidates else 0\n\n    rs = list(range(r0, h, rp))\n    cs = list(range(c0, w, cp))\n    # Each interval between separator lines represents one output cell.\n    rs, cs = rs[:-1], cs[:-1]\n    return [[grid[r][c] if grid[r][c] != fill else fill for c in cs] for r in rs]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"valid":true}},{"step":78,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1793545564.514,"t1":1793545574.894,"alias":"task-4bcb43b3","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT. Wrong attempts so far: 2.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-4bcb43b3\nTest input (27x22):\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 